-- title:
--   In the crossing model, U does not lie in (V)
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring and let $\pi \in W$. Write $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\ W\ \pi$ for the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\ (\mathrm{Fin}\ 2)\ W$, i.e. $W[[X_0,X_1]]$, by the principal ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - \pi$, and let `U π` and `V π` be the two distinguished elements of this quotient ring attached to the two variables. Assume that the quotient ring $W/(\pi)$ is nontrivial, i.e. that $\pi$ is not a unit (equivalently $(\pi) \neq W$). The assertion is that `U π` is not a member of the principal ideal $(\,$`V π`$\,)$ of $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\ W\ \pi$ generated by `V π`; that is, there is no element $f$ of the crossing model with $U = f\,V$. No hypothesis beyond commutativity of $W$ and nontriviality of $W/(\pi)$ is imposed: $\pi$ need not be a nonzerodivisor, nor $W$ local, noetherian or a domain.
--
--   This is the algebraic form of the statement that the two branches through an ordinary double point $uv = \pi$ are incomparable: neither of the two coordinates divides the other in the crossing model. Together with its mirror image it feeds the analysis of the Igusa branches at a node in the study of the supersingular points of the $\Gamma_0(p)$-moduli problem, where it is used to separate the two branch places.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_U_notMem_span_V.lean

